A||||16||Ken Wittlief||'Targa roof line' paint job - jpegs||||3||
Z||000000||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||11:12 PM||||I decided to paint my roof black to bring out the lines of the targa-like roll bar, and give the car a little more unique look.<P>Ive also noticed when a low profile car is coming towards you on the road, with black roof and pillars, its alway a corvette. so I decided to paint the front pillars too.<P>I like the result, I think it will throw people off a little more if they dont know what the car is.<P>for the how to stuff: i wet sanded the clear coat off with 600, masked everything with masking tape and newspaper, and sprayed it in my garage with a can and a half of flat black rustolium. I dusted on the first coat lite, and sprayed three more fairly heavy, till it looked solid and wet. Ive noticed flat black doesnt run very easily. It matches the rest of the flat paint on the car pretty well. I think a matt black would have looked good too.<P>heres the jpgs. I shot them with a Cannon Hi8 camcorder, and captured them on one of my PCs with a WinTV card. For most of the shots the lens was around 5X or 8X or so - I like the way car shots look with long lenses.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/wittlief/c1.jpg">  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/wittlief/c3.jpg">  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/wittlief/c5.jpg">  <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/wittlief/c7.jpg">  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/wittlief/c9.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||11:17 PM||||Ive noticed on the front shot, C5.jpg, the black roof makes the car look even lower than it is - de-emphasizes the roof, and from the front it has a convertable look to it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||06-13-2001||11:21 PM||||Ken....<BR>I like it...  I might do that to the "Smooth GT"...             Steve<P>------------------<BR>Future add's.. 2" drop, 17" wheel's, finish the turbo T-3watercooled project, ViperYellow w/blk racin' stripes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/new_sig_2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||06-13-2001||11:21 PM||||just for location info, thats the historic Erie Canal in some of the shots. It runs right through the middle of Fairport, where we have a 'one of a kind in the world' lift bridge. Its higher on one end than the other, and its higher on the right than it is on the left, and it crosses the canal at an angle, so there is not a single right angle anywhere on the whole bridge.||||reg||1
